---
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import "../styles/legal.css";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | EQUIBT"
  description="How EQUIBT Group collects, uses and protects your personal information, in line with the Australian Privacy Principles."
  canonical="https://www.equibt.com/privacy/"
>
  <Nav />
  <main>
    <section class="legal-hero">
      <div class="legal-wrap">
        <div class="eyebrow">PRIVACY</div>
        <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
        <p class="legal-lead">How we collect, use and protect your personal information.</p>
        <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: 10 July 2026</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-body">
      <div class="legal-wrap legal-prose">
        <p>EQUIBT Group Pty Ltd (ABN 50 044 179 771), trading as EQUIBT ("we", "us", "our"), is committed to protecting your privacy. This policy explains what personal information we collect through this website, how we use it, and the choices you have. We handle personal information in line with the Australian Privacy Principles (APPs) under the <em>Privacy Act 1988</em> (Cth).</p>

        <h2>Information we collect</h2>
        <h3>When you contact us</h3>
        <p>When you submit an enquiry through our contact form, we collect your first and last name, your email address, and the details of your message. You may also choose to give us your phone number and organisation.</p>
        <h3>Automatically when you browse</h3>
        <p>When you use the site, we record limited technical information for security and analytics, including the country your request comes from and your browser type. We do not store your IP address.</p>
        <h3>Analytics and cookies</h3>
        <p>We use Google Analytics 4 and Microsoft Clarity to understand how visitors use the site. These tools use cookies and similar technologies to collect information such as the pages you visit, your device and browser, and a general location (city or country level). This information is aggregated and is not used to identify you personally.</p>
        <h3>Spam protection</h3>
        <p>We use Cloudflare Turnstile to distinguish people from automated bots on our forms. It may process limited technical signals from your browser to do this.</p>

        <h2>How we use your information</h2>
        <p>We use the information we collect to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>respond to your enquiry and assess whether we are the right fit for your needs;</li>
          <li>provide, and communicate with you about, our services;</li>
          <li>maintain the security of the site and prevent misuse; and</li>
          <li>understand and improve how the site performs.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do not sell your personal information, and we do not use it for unrelated marketing without your consent.</p>

        <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
        <p>We use trusted service providers to run this website and communicate with you. They only handle your information to provide their service to us:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — website hosting, database storage, and bot protection;</li>
          <li><strong>Resend</strong> — delivery of the email notifications generated by our contact form;</li>
          <li><strong>Google (Analytics) and Microsoft (Clarity)</strong> — website analytics.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We may also disclose personal information where we are required or authorised to do so by law.</p>

        <h2>Overseas disclosure</h2>
        <p>Some of our service providers store or process information on servers located outside Australia. Where we disclose personal information overseas, we take reasonable steps to ensure it is handled consistently with the Australian Privacy Principles.</p>

        <h2>How we store and protect it</h2>
        <p>Contact enquiries are stored in a secured database hosted by Cloudflare. We take reasonable steps to protect personal information from misuse, loss, and unauthorised access. We keep enquiry details only as long as we need them to respond to you and to maintain our business records, after which we delete or de-identify them.</p>

        <h2>Cookies and how to opt out</h2>
        <p>Most browsers let you refuse or delete cookies through their settings. You can also opt out of Google Analytics using Google's browser opt-out add-on. Blocking cookies may affect how some parts of the site work.</p>

        <h2>Accessing and correcting your information</h2>
        <p>You can ask us for a copy of the personal information we hold about you, or ask us to correct it, at any time. Email <a href="mailto:hello@equibt.com">hello@equibt.com</a> and we will respond within a reasonable period.</p>

        <h2>Complaints</h2>
        <p>If you have a concern about how we have handled your personal information, please contact us first at <a href="mailto:hello@equibt.com">hello@equibt.com</a> so we can try to resolve it. If you are not satisfied with our response, you can contact the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (OAIC) at <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au" target="_blank" rel="noopener">oaic.gov.au</a>.</p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The current version is always available on this page, with the date it was last updated shown at the top.</p>

        <div class="legal-contact">
          <h2>Contact us</h2>
          <p>EQUIBT Group Pty Ltd (ABN 50 044 179 771)<br />Level 15, 470 Collins Street, Melbourne VIC 3000, Australia<br />Email: <a href="mailto:hello@equibt.com">hello@equibt.com</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
